# G6: the stone floor again. The blind reviewer's finding stood after G5's fixes: in
# courses of bevelled bricks the floor read as a wall more than a floor. Redrawn as flagstones
# seen from above: irregular slabs of three tones and different sizes, wrapping, with dark joints
# (no bevel), and a little moss and soil caught in the joints. The joints now are its pattern: any
# layout of slabs leaves rows and columns with more joint in them, so the style guide's repetition
# exception for this tile stays (reworded in style.md).
rect 0,0 24x24 c=stone1 fill
voronoi 0,0 24x24 cells=7 ramp=stone weights=0,0,3,4,1,0 gap=stone1 relax=2 wrap=on seed=34
px 6,13 7,13 8,13 17,9 18,9 c=moss1
px 1,2 2,2 3,2 c=soil1
